[1147 1 "// cyGraph is the graph from the seeds (an object a probe would find held stays out of it), nil past cyMaxNodes."] [1195 1 "// cyRelevant is the nodes a probe must see: those of a strongly connected component with a cycle and a tracked node"] [1196 1 "// (Tarjan's, iterative), and what they reach. An acyclic dead object is Go's to find."] [1289 1 "// cyProbe asks Go's collector which of the nodes in are held from outside the set: the edges between them hidden, a"] [1290 1 "// probe's finalizer on each (a tracked node's own taken off), runtime.GC() with the GIL held, a wait until every"] [1291 1 "// probe ran or Go's finalizers have all run (finBarrier); then the slots put back and the probes taken off. The answer: the nodes"] [1292 1 "// reachable (held from outside, or reached from such a node through the edges)."] [1312 2 "// with its probe set each node outlives its last reference: what an earlier probe held is let go now"] [1400 1 "// cyHideRegistries takes the probed nodes out of the runtime's registries that hold their keys where CPython holds"] [1401 1 "// nothing (queue 241, \"Design: 241\": the weak registries): id()'s identities of untracked objects and the functions'"] [1402 1 "// annotations. The returned function puts back the reachable nodes' entries once the answer is read; the trash's go"] [1403 1 "// (a tracked node's identity into its record), so that Go can free it."] [1437 22 "// the trash's identity in its record, should a finalizer resurrect it"] [1448 1 "// cyDebug (PYI_GC_DEBUG=1): each probe prints to stderr its nodes held from outside that no other probed node holds,"] [1449 1 "// the roots of what it keeps (queue 241: what to look at when a cycle is not found)."] [1484 1 "// cySetFinalizer gives n's object the probe's Go finalizer (a tracked node's own taken off first: Go allows one)."] [1493 1 "// cyRestore gives a surviving tracked node its own Go finalizer again (its record dropped when it needs none)."] [1510 1 "// cyClearWeak